<section class="intro section"><div class="wrap content-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow dark">Start with the source</p><h2>Mold remediation is more than surface cleaning</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Mold is usually a sign that building materials have remained damp. The moisture may come from a roof or plumbing leak, wind driven rain, condensation, foundation seepage, an appliance failure or incomplete drying after water damage. Removing visible growth without finding that cause can lead to repeated damage.</p><p>A practical remediation plan begins by understanding what materials are affected, how far the moisture may have travelled and whether the work area needs containment. Porous materials that are damaged or deeply affected may need to be removed, while sound structural surfaces may be cleaned using an appropriate method.</p><p>West Vancouver properties face a long wet season, varied elevations and many different construction types. Waterfront condos, older homes near established neighbourhoods and complex hillside residences each require a site specific assessment rather than a one size fits all approach.</p></div></div></section>
